From b06a7f55784687cd72418283a1e95b46d4f4a230 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Inochi Amaoto <inochiama@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 02:33:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] riscv: dts: spacemit: k3: Add PCIe controller nodes

The SpacemiT K3 provides five DesignWare PCIe root complexes. Add the
controller and root-port nodes so boards can describe their pinmux, PHY
and slot-supply wiring.

This supersedes the earlier K3 PCIe DTS patch. Compared with that v2
posting, use consistent property ordering and move the PCIe3 secondary
bus range from the controller to its root port, matching the other four
controllers.

This CoM260-focused split intentionally defers the earlier Pico-ITX PCIe
enablement and its board-specific pinctrl groups to a follow-up.

Validation covered clean replay, relaxed DTS style, targeted PCI schema
checks, K3 DTB builds, and the PCIe and combo-PHY objects. No hardware
boot, link training, or endpoint enumeration was performed.

Previous posting:
https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260727094726.890179-3-inochiama@gmail.com

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
